@[expose] public section

/-!
# §6 preamble — the diagram convention for `ℚ`-rational quiver representations

Formalizes the preamble of §6 of `latex/rational_quivers.tex` (census `RQ2-6.04`,
`rmk:repdiagram`), brought into S9's scope on 2026-09-06 by coordinator ruling
**`R-S9-2`** / decision **`D12`** (`PLAN.md` §S9 §1, §5).

## Main results
* `RationalQuivers.Examples.repDiagramConvention` — the two-row diagram convention for `Γ_ℚ`:
  the display's vertex bookkeeping **is** `Γ_ℚ`'s Galois action (`H1`), its horizontal maps are
  `ℚ[√-1]`-linear (`C1`) and its vertical maps `c`-semi-linear (`C2`), and the two conditions the
  source reads off the display are **equivalent** to `eq:semi-linearactiononrep` (`C4`) and
  `eq:koecheractiononrep` (`C3`).
* `RationalQuivers.Examples.repDiagramConvention_cyclic` — "an analogous diagrammatic
  representation exists for the cyclic quiver" (`C5`).

## Why this row is worth a statement, and what its content is

The source's §6 preamble is not decoration: it is what licenses reading the three examples'
displayed diagrams as representations at all, and `RQ2-6.01`–`RQ2-6.03`'s own `…_quiverRep_eq`
statements are stated *against* it. Two of its five clauses are genuine **equivalences** rather
than descriptions —

* `C3`: *"the commutativity of the diagram encodes the compatibility condition
  `eq:koecheractiononrep`"*;
* `C4`: *"the condition `φ_∓ ∘ φ_± = id` and `φ_⋆² = id` corresponds to the cocycle condition
  `eq:semi-linearactiononrep`"*

— and both have real mathematical content, in one direction each way. The display carries data
only at the **non-trivial** Galois element `c`: three vertical maps and four horizontal ones. The
`Rep` axioms (S2, `RQ-1.08-C5`/`C9`) quantify over **all** `σ, τ ∈ Gal(ℚ[√-1]/ℚ)`. The
equivalences say that, for this quadratic extension, the general-`σ` conditions are recovered from
the picture: that is the "encodes"/"corresponds to" the source asserts, and it is what would fail
if the display omitted something.

## Implementation notes

**The statement quantifies over raw display data, not over a `Rep`.** A `Rep (gelfandQ …)` already
*carries* the cocycle and edge-equivariance conditions as fields, so an equivalence stated of one
would have a true right-hand side and would collapse to its left-hand side — a degenerate reading
G2 forbids. The data below is therefore a bare family `M : Fin 3 → Type` with the display's own
maps, and the equivalences are between two conditions on it, neither of which is assumed.

**Everything is stated in the disjoint union `⊔_v M(v)`**, i.e. as equalities in `(v : Fin 3) × M v`.
This is S2's own device (`Quiver/Rep/Basic.lean`, "the dependent-type crux"): `φ_{v,σ}` goes
`M(v) → M(σ·v)`, so both conditions compare maps whose codomains agree only propositionally, and
the sigma-typed reading is the same equation with no `cast` in it. `Rep.cocycle` and
`Rep.edge_equivariance` are stated in exactly this form, so the right-hand sides below are those
two fields verbatim rather than a re-rendering of them.

`(gelfandQ Qi.card_gal).V` reduces to `Fin 3` and `.E` to `Fin 4` (`RQuiver.gelfand` is
`@[reducible]`), and `c` acts on both by the `±`-swap (`Examples.gelfandQ_smul_vertex`,
`…_smul_edge`), which is why `RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap` and `RQuiver.gelfandEdgeSwap` are the
display's own bookkeeping and the first conjunct can pin them to `Γ_ℚ`'s action.
-/

namespace RationalQuivers.Examples

open RationalQuivers.HC RationalQuivers.Gelfand CategoryTheory
open RationalQuivers.Gelfand.RationalStructure (vtxQ edgeQ)
open RationalQuivers.Gelfand.Cyclic (vtxC edgeC)

/-! ## The action the display's vertical maps generate -/

open scoped Classical in
/-- The `Gal(ℚ[√-1]/ℚ)`-action generated by the display's three vertical maps, read on the
disjoint union `⊔_{v} M(v)`: the identity at `1`, and the display's own `φ_•` at `c`.  This is the
whole of the action the picture carries — the point of clauses `RQ2-6.04-C3`/`C4` is that it is
enough.  @census none (helper) -/
noncomputable def displayAct {M : Fin 3 → Type} [∀ v, AddCommGroup (M v)]
    (vert : ∀ v : Fin 3, M v ≃+ M (RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap v))
    (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (x : (v : Fin 3) × M v) : (v : Fin 3) × M v :=
  if σ = 1 then x else ⟨RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap x.1, vert x.1 x.2⟩

open scoped Classical in
/-- The same for the cyclic quiver's two-node display.  @census none (helper) -/
noncomputable def displayActC {M : Fin 2 → Type} [∀ v, AddCommGroup (M v)]
    (vert : ∀ v : Fin 2, M v ≃+ M (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm v))
    (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (x : (v : Fin 2) × M v) : (v : Fin 2) × M v :=
  if σ = 1 then x else ⟨RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm x.1, vert x.1 x.2⟩

/-! ## The convention -/

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false in
/-- **`RQ2-6.04`** (§6 preamble) — the two-row diagram convention for `ℚ`-rational representations
of the Gelfand quiver `Γ_ℚ`.

A display consists of a family `M = (M(−), M(⋆), M(+))` of `ℚ[√-1]`-vector spaces, four horizontal
maps `φ_{a_∓}, φ_{b_∓}` along the edges of `ex:gelfand`, and three vertical maps `φ_−, φ_⋆, φ_+`
from each vertex to its `c`-image.  The source asserts four things about it, and this is all four:

* **`H1`** — the display is a display *of `Γ_ℚ`*: the vertex bookkeeping it uses, `v ↦ c·v` by the
  `±`-swap, **is** the Galois action of the `ℚ`-rational Gelfand quiver (**first** conjunct).
* **`C1`** — the horizontal maps are `ℚ[√-1]`-**linear**: carried by the type of `hor`,
  `M(s(e)) →ₗ[ℚ[√-1]] M(t(e))`, so no display without it can be formed.
* **`C2`** — the vertical maps are **semi-linear** for complex conjugation `c`: the hypothesis
  `hsemi` at `c`, together with the **second** conjunct, which propagates it to the whole generated
  action — `displayAct vert σ` is `σ`-semi-linear for **every** `σ`, which is S2's `Rep.semilinear`
  field (`RQ-1.08-C4`) and is the form `eq:koecheractiononrep`'s ambient setting needs.
* **`C4`** — `φ_∓ ∘ φ_± = id` and `φ_⋆² = id`, read on the display, is **equivalent** to the
  cocycle condition `eq:semi-linearactiononrep` (S2's `Rep.cocycle`, clause `RQ-1.08-C5`) for the
  action the display generates (**third** conjunct).
* **`C3`** — commutativity of the display's four squares is **equivalent** to the compatibility
  condition `eq:koecheractiononrep` (S2's `Rep.edge_equivariance`, clause `RQ-1.08-C9`) (**fourth**
  conjunct).

Both equivalences are stated in the disjoint union, which is the form S2's two fields themselves
take; the `←` directions are instantiation at `σ = τ = c`, and the `→` directions are the content:
that a picture carrying data only at `c` determines the conditions at every `σ`.

@census    RQ2-6.04
@source    rmk:repdiagram
@clauses   RQ2-6.04-H1, RQ2-6.04-C1, RQ2-6.04-C2, RQ2-6.04-C3, RQ2-6.04-C4
@imports   none
@divergence none.  `C1` is carried **structurally**, by `hor`'s type `M(s(e)) →ₗ[ℚ[√-1]] M(t(e))`:
no display lacking it can be formed, so it cannot be dropped by a later edit.

`C2` is carried by the hypothesis `hsemi` **and consumed by the second conjunct**.  The earlier
wording claimed the hypothesis form was "strictly stronger than asserting", which finding
`V-S9G2-3` correctly refuted: `hsemi` was a **dead binder** — the three original conjuncts hold for
an arbitrary additive `vert`, by case analysis on the two-element Galois group — and a hypothesis
no conclusion consumes narrows the theorem without adding content (the `V-S8-13(d)` shape).  The
repair is not to delete it but to state what the source actually asserts and what `hsemi` is for:
semi-linearity of the **generated action at every `σ`**.  That conjunct is **equivalent** to
`hsemi` (two-element group); stated so the display's vertical data is visibly `Rep.semilinear`.
It is not derivable from the other three conjuncts, so the binder is genuinely live; it is **not**
stronger than `hsemi`, and the earlier claim that it was is corrected here (finding `V-S9D1-1`,
class 7, `VERIFICATION-DELTA-1.md` §3, probe `P8b`: the conjunct's `σ = c` instance returns
`hsemi`, and its `σ = 1` instance is trivial).

The two equivalences are stated of the *generated* action
`displayAct` rather than of an abstract `Rep`, because a `Rep` carries both conditions as fields
and an equivalence with a field on one side would be degenerate; see the module's implementation
notes. -/
theorem repDiagramConvention
    (M : Fin 3 → Type) [∀ v, AddCommGroup (M v)] [∀ v, Module (Qi : Type) (M v)]
    (vert : ∀ v : Fin 3, M v ≃+ M (RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap v))
    (hor : ∀ e : Fin 4,
      M (RQuiver.gelfand.source e) →ₗ[(Qi : Type)] M (RQuiver.gelfand.target e))
    (hsemi : ∀ (v : Fin 3) (a : (Qi : Type)) (m : M v),
      vert v (a • m) = galConj a • vert v m) :
    -- `H1`: the display's vertex bookkeeping IS `Γ_ℚ`'s Galois action
    (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (v : Fin 3) (m : M v),
        (displayAct vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).1 = σ • (vtxQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal v)) ∧
    -- `C2`: the generated action is `σ`-semi-linear at EVERY `σ`, not only at `c` — S2's
    -- `Rep.semilinear` (`RQ-1.08-C4`).  This is the conjunct that consumes `hsemi`.
    (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (v : Fin 3) (a : (Qi : Type)) (m : M v),
        displayAct vert σ ⟨v, a • m⟩
          = ⟨(displayAct vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).1, σ a • (displayAct vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).2⟩) ∧
    -- `C4`: `φ_∓φ_± = id`, `φ_⋆² = id`  ⟺  `eq:semi-linearactiononrep`
    ((∀ (v : Fin 3) (m : M v),
        displayAct vert galConj (displayAct vert galConj ⟨v, m⟩) = ⟨v, m⟩)
      ↔ (∀ (σ τ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (x : (v : Fin 3) × M v),
        displayAct vert σ (displayAct vert τ x) = displayAct vert (σ * τ) x)) ∧
    -- `C3`: the four squares of the display commute  ⟺  `eq:koecheractiononrep`
    ((∀ (e : Fin 4) (m : M (RQuiver.gelfand.source e))
        (m' : M (RQuiver.gelfand.source (RQuiver.gelfandEdgeSwap e))),
        (⟨RQuiver.gelfand.source (RQuiver.gelfandEdgeSwap e), m'⟩ : (v : Fin 3) × M v)
            = displayAct vert galConj ⟨RQuiver.gelfand.source e, m⟩ →
          (⟨RQuiver.gelfand.target (RQuiver.gelfandEdgeSwap e),
              hor (RQuiver.gelfandEdgeSwap e) m'⟩ : (v : Fin 3) × M v)
            = displayAct vert galConj ⟨RQuiver.gelfand.target e, hor e m⟩)
      ↔ (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (e : Fin 4) (m : M (RQuiver.gelfand.source e))
          (m' : M (RQuiver.gelfand.source (σ • edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e))),
        (⟨RQuiver.gelfand.source (σ • edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e), m'⟩ : (v : Fin 3) × M v)
            = displayAct vert σ ⟨RQuiver.gelfand.source e, m⟩ →
          (⟨RQuiver.gelfand.target (σ • edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e),
              hor (σ • edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e) m'⟩ : (v : Fin 3) × M v)
            = displayAct vert σ ⟨RQuiver.gelfand.target e, hor e m⟩)) := by
  have hone : ∀ x : (v : Fin 3) × M v, displayAct vert 1 x = x := by
    intro x; simp [displayAct]
  have hne : ∀ {σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)}, σ ≠ 1 → ∀ x : (v : Fin 3) × M v,
      displayAct vert σ x = ⟨RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap x.1, vert x.1 x.2⟩ := by
    intro σ hσ x; simp only [displayAct, if_neg hσ]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- `H1`: the display's vertex bookkeeping is `Γ_ℚ`'s Galois action
    intro σ v m
    rw [gelfandQ_smul_eq]
    by_cases hσ : σ = 1
    · subst hσ; rw [hone]; simp
    · rw [hne hσ, if_neg hσ]
  · -- `C2`: the generated action is `σ`-semi-linear at every `σ` (probe `P8a`)
    intro σ v a m
    by_cases hσ : σ = 1
    · subst hσ; rw [hone, hone]; rfl
    · rw [hne hσ, hne hσ]
      show (⟨RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap v, vert v (a • m)⟩ : (w : Fin 3) × M w)
        = ⟨RQuiver.gelfandVertexSwap v, σ a • vert v m⟩
      rw [hsemi, eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ]
  · -- `C4`: `φ_∓φ_± = id`, `φ_⋆² = id`  ⟺  the cocycle condition at every `σ, τ`
    constructor
    · intro h σ τ x
      obtain ⟨v, m⟩ := x
      by_cases hσ : σ = 1
      · subst hσ; rw [hone, one_mul]
      · by_cases hτ : τ = 1
        · subst hτ; rw [hone, mul_one]
        · rw [eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ, eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hτ,
            galConj_mul_self, hone]
          exact h v m
    · intro h v m
      have hx := h galConj galConj ⟨v, m⟩
      rwa [galConj_mul_self, hone] at hx
  · -- `C3`: the four squares commute  ⟺  edge-equivariance at every `σ`
    constructor
    · intro h σ e m
      by_cases hσ : σ = 1
      · subst hσ
        rw [show (1 : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) • edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e
              = edgeQ SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e from one_smul _ _]
        intro m' hm'
        rw [hone] at hm' ⊢
        obtain ⟨-, hsnd⟩ := Sigma.mk.inj hm'
        rw [eq_of_heq hsnd]
      · rw [eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ, gelfandQ_smul_edge]
        exact h e m
    · intro h e m m' hm'
      have hx := h galConj e m
      rw [gelfandQ_smul_edge] at hx
      exact hx m' hm'

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false in
/-- **`RQ2-6.04-C5`** — "an analogous diagrammatic representation exists for the cyclic quiver":
the same two equivalences for `ex:cyclic`'s two-node display, whose Galois bookkeeping is the
two-element swap (`Gelfand.Cyclic.cyclicQ_smul_vertex`, `…_smul_edge`).

@census    none (auxiliary; discharges census clause `RQ2-6.04-C5`)
@source    rmk:repdiagram
@clauses   RQ2-6.04-C5
@imports   none
@divergence JUSTIFIED_REFORMULATION (the census's own reading, `if_missing =
JUSTIFIED_REFORMULATION` on this clause).  The source says only "an analogous diagrammatic
representation exists for the cyclic quiver", without drawing it or stating what "analogous"
quantifies over.  Rendered as: the identical pair of equivalences, with `Fin 3`/`gelfandVertexSwap`
/`gelfandEdgeSwap` replaced by `Fin 2`/`twoLoopsSwapPerm` throughout and the four edges by the
cyclic quiver's two — which is what "analogous" can only mean, and which is the form `RQ2-6.02`'s
`ℓ = 0` diagram (`D_zero_quiverRep_eq`) is read against.  As in the Gelfand case, `hsemi` is
consumed by the semi-linearity conjunct (finding `V-S9G2-3`), not left as a dead binder. -/
theorem repDiagramConvention_cyclic
    (M : Fin 2 → Type) [∀ v, AddCommGroup (M v)] [∀ v, Module (Qi : Type) (M v)]
    (vert : ∀ v : Fin 2, M v ≃+ M (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm v))
    (hor : ∀ e : Fin 2,
      M (RQuiver.cyclic.source e) →ₗ[(Qi : Type)] M (RQuiver.cyclic.target e))
    (hsemi : ∀ (v : Fin 2) (a : (Qi : Type)) (m : M v),
      vert v (a • m) = galConj a • vert v m) :
    (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (v : Fin 2) (m : M v),
        (displayActC vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).1 = σ • (vtxC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal v)) ∧
    (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (v : Fin 2) (a : (Qi : Type)) (m : M v),
        displayActC vert σ ⟨v, a • m⟩
          = ⟨(displayActC vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).1, σ a • (displayActC vert σ ⟨v, m⟩).2⟩) ∧
    ((∀ (v : Fin 2) (m : M v),
        displayActC vert galConj (displayActC vert galConj ⟨v, m⟩) = ⟨v, m⟩)
      ↔ (∀ (σ τ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (x : (v : Fin 2) × M v),
        displayActC vert σ (displayActC vert τ x) = displayActC vert (σ * τ) x)) ∧
    ((∀ (e : Fin 2) (m : M (RQuiver.cyclic.source e))
        (m' : M (RQuiver.cyclic.source (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm e))),
        (⟨RQuiver.cyclic.source (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm e), m'⟩ : (v : Fin 2) × M v)
            = displayActC vert galConj ⟨RQuiver.cyclic.source e, m⟩ →
          (⟨RQuiver.cyclic.target (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm e),
              hor (RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm e) m'⟩ : (v : Fin 2) × M v)
            = displayActC vert galConj ⟨RQuiver.cyclic.target e, hor e m⟩)
      ↔ (∀ (σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) (e : Fin 2) (m : M (RQuiver.cyclic.source e))
          (m' : M (RQuiver.cyclic.source (σ • edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e))),
        (⟨RQuiver.cyclic.source (σ • edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e), m'⟩ : (v : Fin 2) × M v)
            = displayActC vert σ ⟨RQuiver.cyclic.source e, m⟩ →
          (⟨RQuiver.cyclic.target (σ • edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e),
              hor (σ • edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e) m'⟩ : (v : Fin 2) × M v)
            = displayActC vert σ ⟨RQuiver.cyclic.target e, hor e m⟩)) := by
  have hone : ∀ x : (v : Fin 2) × M v, displayActC vert 1 x = x := by
    intro x; simp [displayActC]
  have hne : ∀ {σ : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)}, σ ≠ 1 → ∀ x : (v : Fin 2) × M v,
      displayActC vert σ x = ⟨RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm x.1, vert x.1 x.2⟩ := by
    intro σ hσ x; simp only [displayActC, if_neg hσ]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro σ v m
    rw [cyclicQ_smul_eq]
    by_cases hσ : σ = 1
    · subst hσ; rw [hone]; simp
    · rw [hne hσ, if_neg hσ]
  · intro σ v a m
    by_cases hσ : σ = 1
    · subst hσ; rw [hone, hone]; rfl
    · rw [hne hσ, hne hσ]
      show (⟨RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm v, vert v (a • m)⟩ : (w : Fin 2) × M w)
        = ⟨RQuiver.twoLoopsSwapPerm v, σ a • vert v m⟩
      rw [hsemi, eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ]
  · constructor
    · intro h σ τ x
      obtain ⟨v, m⟩ := x
      by_cases hσ : σ = 1
      · subst hσ; rw [hone, one_mul]
      · by_cases hτ : τ = 1
        · subst hτ; rw [hone, mul_one]
        · rw [eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ, eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hτ,
            galConj_mul_self, hone]
          exact h v m
    · intro h v m
      have hx := h galConj galConj ⟨v, m⟩
      rwa [galConj_mul_self, hone] at hx
  · constructor
    · intro h σ e m
      by_cases hσ : σ = 1
      · subst hσ
        rw [show (1 : (Qi : Type) ≃ₐ[ℚ] (Qi : Type)) • edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e
              = edgeC SqrtNegOneExt.qi.card_gal e from one_smul _ _]
        intro m' hm'
        rw [hone] at hm' ⊢
        obtain ⟨-, hsnd⟩ := Sigma.mk.inj hm'
        rw [eq_of_heq hsnd]
      · rw [eq_galConj_of_ne_one Qi.card_gal hσ, cyclicQ_smul_edge]
        exact h e m
    · intro h e m m' hm'
      have hx := h galConj e m
      rw [cyclicQ_smul_edge] at hx
      exact hx m' hm'

end RationalQuivers.Examples
